Brainstorm a plan for "$ARGUMENTS" using {{ CLI_NAME }} patterns.

1. Explore the project context:
   - Check recent commits, existing files, and docs.
   - Run `{{ CLI_NAME }} pattern search -q "$ARGUMENTS"` to see if any
     patterns already relate to this area.

2. Ask the user clarifying questions — one at a time — to understand:
   - What they are trying to achieve
   - What constraints apply
   - What success looks like

3. Identify the key intents (topics, domains, capabilities) this plan touches.
   For each intent, run `{{ CLI_NAME }} pattern search -q "<intent>"` to
   understand what patterns already exist.

4. From the search results, determine:
   - Which existing patterns can be reused for this plan
   - Which new patterns would need to be created
   - What work doesn't fit a pattern (one-off tasks)

5. Present the plan in sections, covering:
   - Overview of the approach
   - Existing patterns to reuse (with names)
   - New patterns to create (with suggested names and intents)
   - Non-pattern work (one-off tasks)
   - Suggested order of implementation

6. Get user approval on the plan before proceeding.

7. Once approved, save the plan to a spec file (e.g.
   `docs/superpowers/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md`) and commit it.
   Then transition to creating an implementation plan.